From: Nestor <nestor@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dsi: exact link rate for non-burst video

Bridges like the TC358762 on the Raspberry Pi 7-inch screen rebuild the pixel
timing from the DSI link rate, so a non-burst video link must run at exactly
the pixel data rate; the usual 25% extra left the picture shifted and its
colours a byte off on the ASUS Tinker Board.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw-mipi-dsi-rockchip.c
@@ -573,8 +573,18 @@
 
 	mpclk = DIV_ROUND_UP(mode->clock, MSEC_PER_SEC);
 	if (mpclk) {
-		/* take 1 / 0.8, since mbps must big than bandwidth of RGB */
-		tmp = mpclk * (bpp / lanes) * 10 / 8;
+		/*
+		 * Non-burst video: bridges like the TC358762 (Raspberry Pi 7-inch
+		 * screen) rebuild the pixel timing from the link rate, so it must
+		 * be exactly the pixel data rate. Otherwise take 1 / 0.8, since
+		 * mbps must big than bandwidth of RGB.
+		 */
+		if ((mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO) &&
+		    !(mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST))
+			tmp = DIV_ROUND_UP(mode->clock * (bpp / lanes),
+					   MSEC_PER_SEC);
+		else
+			tmp = mpclk * (bpp / lanes) * 10 / 8;
 		if (tmp < max_mbps)
 			target_mbps = tmp;
 		else
